The `TokenBucket` struct provides a simple token bucket algorithm for tracking the number of requests that can be made within a given time window. It uses a fixed capacity buffer to store the number of tokens available, and it discards any tokens that are not used within a given time window.
```rust
// token_bucket.rs
pub struct TokenBucket {
    capacity: usize,
    tokens: Vec<Token>,
}

impl TokenBucket {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self { capacity: 10, tokens: vec![] }
    }

    pub async fn add_tokens(&mut self, token: &str) {
        // Add a new token to the buffer
        self.tokens.push(Token::new(token));

        // Discard any expired tokens
        let now = std::time::Instant::now();
        self.tokens.retain(|token| !token.is_expired(now));
    }
}
```
