The `Token` struct represents a single token in the token bucket. It has an expiration timestamp and a value, which is the actual token.
```rust
// token.rs
pub struct Token {
    expires_at: std::time::Instant,
    value: String,
}

impl Token {
    pub fn new(value: &str) -> Self {
        let duration = Duration::from_secs(1); // 1 second expiration time
        let now = std::time::Instant::now();
        let expires_at = now + duration;

        Self { expires_at, value: value.to_string() }
    }

    pub fn is_expired(&self, now: std::time::Instant) -> bool {
        self.expires_at < now
    }
}
```
