The code also sets up a timeout mechanism for long-running processes using the `child_process` module's `exec` method with the `timeout` option set to a non-zero value. This will cause the child process to be killed if it does not complete within the specified time period. The `exit` event is also listened to in case the process exits without completing successfully, in which case an error message is sent back to the client.

