To make this code more scalable, fault-tolerant, and cost-efficient, we can implement asynchronous processing pipelines, automated failover mechanisms, and other features that enable us to process high-velocity streams of geospatial data in near-real-time while minimizing latency and maximizing throughput. Additionally, we can use managed vs. unmanaged services for enhanced control and performance tuning, evaluate the trade-offs between these options, and ensure data consistency across distributed databases. Finally, we can optimize for user privacy and data protection through robust security measures and provide detailed logging and observability tools for monitoring and debugging."]

