This code uses the `EventHubClient` class to read messages from an event hub, deserialize them into JSON objects, and extract the sensor data. It then checks if the sensor data has already been processed by checking if it exists in a cache of previously processed data points. If the data point has not been processed, it is inserted into a time series database using the `TimeSeriesDatabaseClient` class. The code also includes retry logic for failed inserts to handle transient failures in the time series database.

