* `token_`: The access token obtained from the API.
* `refresh_token_`: The refresh token used to renew the access token.
* `expires_in_`: The number of seconds remaining before the access token expires.
* `last_access_`: The timestamp when the access token was last accessed.
* `renewal_threshold_`: The threshold for renewing the access token, in seconds.

The class also has a `renewToken()` method that renews the access token using the refresh token and updates the expiration time. It uses the cURL library to make an HTTP POST request to the API endpoint and parses the response as JSON.

The `writeCallback` function is called by cURL whenever data is received from the server during the HTTP request. It writes the response to a json object and updates the access token, refresh token, and expiration time accordingly.

