The `CacheEntry` struct stores the request and response objects, along with a timestamp for LRU eviction. The `LRUEviction` class maintains a map of timestamps to cache entries and removes the least recently used entry from the map when necessary.

The `HighPerformanceHttpCache` class provides methods to add HTTP requests and responses, retrieve cached responses, and remove the least recently used entry from the cache. It also supports thread safety using a mutex.']

