    private static final String KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS = "localhost:9092";
    private static final String KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP_ID = "log-processing-service";
    private static final String KAFKA_TOPIC = "logs";
    private static final String REDIS_MASTER_NAME = "mymaster";
    private static final String REDIS_SENTINEL_HOST = "localhost";
    private static final int REDIS_SENTINEL_PORT = 26379;
    private static final String REDIS_PASSWORD = "redis-password";

    public void start() {
        // Create Kafka consumer properties
        Map<String, Object> consumerProperties = new HashMap<>();
        consumerProperties.put(ConsumerConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG, KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS);
        consumerProperties.put(ConsumerConfig.GROUP_ID_CONFIG, KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP_ID);
        consumerProperties.put(ConsumerConfig.KEY_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, StringDeserializer.class);
        consumerProperties.put(ConsumerConfig.VALUE_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, StringDeserializer.class);

        // Create Redis sentinel pool configuration
        JedisSentinelPool sentinelPool = new JedisSentinelPool(REDIS_MASTER_NAME, REDIS_SENTINEL_HOST + ":" + REDIS_SENTINEL_PORT, 2000, 3, new JedisPoolConfig(), REDIS_PASSWORD);

        // Create Spark streaming context
        JavaStreamingContext ssc = new JavaStreamingContext(consumerProperties, "log-processing-service");

        // Create Kafka stream for log messages
        JavaInputDStream<String> kafkaStream = KafkaUtils.createDirectStream(ssc, String.class, String.class, StringDeserializer.class, StringDeserializer.class, consumerProperties, KAFKA_TOPIC);

        // Transform log messages into key-value pairs for encryption and decryption
        JavaDStream<String> logMessages = kafkaStream.map(message -> {
            // Extract log message fields and perform any necessary preprocessing
            String[] fields = message.split("\\|");
            return new Tuple2<>(fields[0], fields[1]);
        });

        // Encrypt and forward log messages to Redis sentinel pool
        logMessages.foreachRDD(rdd -> {
            rdd.foreachPartition(partition -> {
                JedisSentinelPool sentinelPool = new JedisSentinelPool(REDIS_MASTER_NAME, REDIS_SENTINEL_HOST + ":" + REDIS_SENTINEL_PORT, 2000, 3, new JedisPoolConfig(), REDIS_PASSWORD);
                try (Jedis jedis = sentinelPool.getResource()) {
                    // Encrypt log message using AES-GCM and encode as Base64 string
                    Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
                    cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, new SecretKeySpec("your-secret-key".getBytes(), "AES"));
                    GCMParameterSpec parameterSpec = cipher.getParameters().getParameterSpec(GCMParameterSpec.class);
                    byte[] encryptedMessage = cipher.doFinal(partition.iterator().next());
                    String encodedMessage = Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(encryptedMessage);

                    // Forward encrypted message to Redis sentinel pool for storage
                    jedis.set("log-message", encodedMessage);
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    System.err.println("Error encountered during encryption and forwarding of log messages: " + e);
                }
            });
        });

        // Start Spark streaming context
        ssc.start();
        ssc.awaitTermination();
    }
}
```
This code defines a `LogProcessingService` class that implements the high-traffic, real-time log processing service for an e-commerce platform with multi-tenant support. The service uses Apache Kafka as the event streaming platform and Redis Sentinel for data storage and retrieval.

The service starts by creating a Kafka consumer properties map with relevant configuration settings such as the bootstrap servers, group ID, key deserializer, value deserializer, and topic. It then creates a Spark streaming context using these properties and defines a Kafka stream for log messages.

The `foreachRDD` method is used to perform the encryption and forwarding of log messages to Redis Sentinel pool for storage. The method first extracts the log message fields and performs any necessary preprocessing. It then initializes the AES-GCM cipher with a secret key using the `Cipher.getInstance()` method, encrypts the log message using the `doFinal()` method, encodes the encrypted message as a Base64 string using the `Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString()` method, and forwards the encoded message to Redis Sentinel pool using the `set()` method.

The service starts the Spark streaming context and waits for termination. The service is designed to handle high-traffic data ingestion and encryption of log messages in real-time, ensuring a secure and scalable data storage solution for the e-commerce platform.']

