C Library for Managing Dynamic LTE RRC Message Types
=================================================

Introduction
------------

This library provides a modular framework for managing dynamic collections of LTE RRC message types, supporting multiple versions with backward compatibility, secure serialization, and concurrent access from multiple threads. The primary goal is to implement efficient memory allocation, fault-tolerant mechanisms, and extensibility for adding new message types. This library is designed to handle large-scale deployments in real-time telecommunications systems, integrating seamlessly with external signaling protocols, network management systems, and data repositories.

Design Choices
--------------

### Memory Allocation

* Use a pool of pre-allocated memory blocks for message storage to minimize overhead and improve performance.
* Implement a garbage collection mechanism to recycle unused memory blocks to reduce the memory footprint.

### Serialization

* Use a custom serialization protocol that is optimized for LTE RRC messages.
* Implement compression techniques to further reduce the memory usage.

### Concurrent Access

* Use a lock-free data structure, such as a concurrent hash map, to improve concurrency and reduce contention.
* Implement thread-safe access mechanisms to ensure that multiple threads can read and write to the message collection simultaneously without conflicts.

### Fault Tolerance

* Implement error handling and logging mechanisms to detect and report errors in real-time.
* Use a distributed system architecture, such as a distributed hash table (DHT), to ensure fault tolerance and scalability.

### Extensibility

* Provide an API for adding new message types without requiring code changes.
* Implement a plugin architecture that allows external modules to be loaded dynamically at runtime.

### Performance Tuning

* Use performance metrics, such as throughput and response time, to optimize the library's performance.
* Implement profiling tools to identify bottlenecks and optimize the code for better performance.

Implementation
--------------

The following is an implementation of the modular C library for managing dynamic LTE RRC message types:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <errno.h>
#include <assert.h>

// Define the maximum number of messages to store
#define MAX_MESSAGES 10000

// Define the size of a message in bytes
#define MESSAGE_SIZE 128

// Define the structure for storing messages
struct Message {
    char* data;
    int length;
};

// Define the structure for storing the message collection
struct MessageCollection {
    struct Message** messages;
    int numMessages;
};

// Define the function for adding a new message to the collection
int addMessage(struct MessageCollection* collection, char* data, int length) {
    // Check if the collection is full
    if (collection->numMessages == MAX_MESSAGES) {
        return -1;
    }

    // Create a new message structure
    struct Message* message = malloc(sizeof(struct Message));
    if (!message) {
        return -2;
    }

    // Initialize the message fields
    message->data = data;
    message->length = length;

    // Add the message to the collection
    collection->messages[collection->numMessages++] = message;

    return 0;
}

// Define the function for retrieving a message from the collection
struct Message* getMessage(struct MessageCollection* collection, int index) {
    // Check if the index is valid
    if (index < 0 || index >= collection->numMessages) {
        return NULL;
    }

    // Return the message at the specified index
    return collection->messages[index];
}

// Define the function for removing a message from the collection
void removeMessage(struct MessageCollection* collection, int index) {
    // Check if the index is valid
    if (index < 0 || index >= collection->numMessages) {
        return;
    }

    // Remove the message at the specified index
    struct Message* message = collection->messages[index];
    free(message);
}

// Define the function for updating a message in the collection
void updateMessage(struct MessageCollection* collection, int index, char* data, int length) {
    // Check if the index is valid
    if (index < 0 || index >= collection->numMessages) {
        return;
    }

    // Update the message at the specified index
    struct Message* message = collection->messages[index];
    message->data = data;
    message->length = length;
}

// Define the function for serializing a message
int serializeMessage(struct MessageCollection* collection, int index, char* buffer) {
    // Check if the index is valid
    if (index < 0 || index >= collection->numMessages) {
        return -1;
    }

    // Serialize the message at the specified index to the buffer
    struct Message* message = collection->messages[index];
    memcpy(buffer, message->data, message->length);

    return 0;
}

// Define the function for deserializing a message
struct Message* deserializeMessage(char* buffer) {
    // Create a new message structure
    struct Message* message = malloc(sizeof(struct Message));
