This code uses a shared pointer (`std::shared_ptr`) to manage memory and avoids using raw pointers. It also uses `std::atomic` to implement thread-safe operations and `std::mutex` to synchronize access to shared data. The `std::condition_variable` is used to wait for completion of tasks in a non-blocking way.

This code is a simple example of how to implement an asynchronous request processor using threads. It may not be suitable for all use cases, and more complex implementations may be needed for certain applications.']

