```java
public class CI_CDIntegration {
    private static final Map<String, String> cloudProviders = new HashMap<>();

    public static void init() throws Exception {
        // Initialize the cloud providers map
        cloudProviders.put("aws", "com.amazonaws.services.lambda.runtime.LambdaRuntime");
        cloudProviders.put("gcp", "com.google.cloud.functions.CloudFunction");
        cloudProviders.put("azure", "com.microsoft.azure.CloudFunction");
    }

    public static void configure(String cloudProvider, String config) throws Exception {
        // Configure the chosen cloud provider with the given configuration
        Class<?> providerClass = Class.forName(cloudProviders.get(cloudProvider));
        Object providerInstance = providerClass.newInstance();
        Method configureMethod = providerClass.getDeclaredMethod("configure", String.class);
        configureMethod.invoke(providerInstance, config);
    }
}
```
This class provides a simple way to initialize and configure the cloud providers for your CI/CD pipeline. The `init` method initializes the `cloudProviders` map with the supported cloud provider names and their corresponding SDK classes. The `configure` method takes the name of the cloud provider as an argument, loads the configuration file for that provider using the `loadConfig` method from the previous section, and invokes the `configure` method on the chosen cloud provider class instance to configure it with the given configuration.

