We have also created factories for each of these classes that can create instances of the classes using the host and port information. These factories are useful when we need to create multiple instances of the same class with different configuration parameters.

In addition, we have created a `NetworkServiceManager` class that can start a network service using TLS/SSL and manage its lifecycle. This class is useful when we need to start a network service for each client request and shut it down after processing the request.']

